{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A minimum cycle basis (de Pina 1995): "},{"code":"edgeCount - vertexCount + c","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" cycles, for c"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"components, independent over GF(2) and spanning the cycle space, with the fewest edges in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"total of any such basis. Self-loops and parallel edges are supported: a loop is a cycle of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its own, and two copies of an edge form a cycle of length 2. Each cycle starts at its least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order and leaves it through the lesser of its two edges there; the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cycles come in nondecreasing length, then by their edge positions. Ties between equally"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"short cycles are broken by the rows’ order."}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","symbolKind":"method","title":"minimumCycleBasis()","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Cycles\/MinimumCycleBasis.swift#L216","fileName":"MinimumCycleBasis.swift"},"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6CyclesE17minimumCycleBasisSay5Walks0E0Vy6VertexQz5Edges_5IndexQZGGyF","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumCycleBasis","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks5CycleV","text":"Cycle","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphPr